  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nClosed upper high will linger over the northern high plains the\nfirst part of this week, keeping the heat going over the Dakotas\nand into our SE zones through Wednesday. Heat Warnings were\ntrimmed for tomorrow to just Prairie and Wibaux counties. Daniels\nand Sheridan counties drop out of the Advisory tomorrow with an\nadvisory for the remainder of the zones.\n\nThen an upper disturbance sends storms northeast into the CWA\nabout 03z. Updraft helicity and Max Updraft from the HREF is\nshowing severe thundertorm potential for the western zones. With\nthe high Precip Waters (1.0 to 1.8\"), flooding could also be a \nconcern. Will go ahead and issue a Flash Flood Watch for the\nPetroleum and Phillips counties.\n\nWednesday and beyond: Upper low over the Pacific NW then moves NE\ninto the Prairie Provinces of Canada while the upper ridge \nrebounds over eastern Montana. This should keep temps warmer than \nnormal with small chances for showers and storms. TFJ\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nGnerally did not deviate from NBM, but did lower Min RH for today\na bit. TFJ",
